{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Difficult Relationships"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Appointment"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le08ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Perfect Modals: Could Have"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to express uncertainty about past events, you can use the Perfect modal phrase <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "  You use <span class=\"italic\">could have</span> + past participle to:<br/>  <ul><li>talk about the fact that you had the ability or opportunity to do something in the past, but didn't do it. <br/> For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">could have gone</span> to that University, but I didn't want to.</span></li>  <li>talk about a suggestion that was not taken<br/>  For example:<br/>   <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">could have asked</span> the boss to give you a different task.</span>  <br/> <li>talk about an action that almost happened, but didn't.<br/>  For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Watch out! That bicycle <span class=\"strong\">could have hit</span> you!</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Alex wondered how he and Jennifer could have managed to stay happily married all these years."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He decided that his wife could have arrived at the bank exactly on time and then left."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You could have waited a little longer."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You couldn't have been there."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Non-Finite Clauses with -<span class=\"italic\">ing</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you think of a clause, you think of it having its own subject and verb. There are cases, however, when the clause does not contain a main verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "These are examples of non-defining clauses and the two clauses have the same subject:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>Actions happening at the same time<br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Waving their hats and shouting</span>, the fans ran onto the field.  </span></li><br/> <li>One action happening before another <br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Opening the envelope</span>, she found that it contained a cheque for $1,000.  </span><br/><br/> You often explain the <span class=\"strong\">reason for something happening</span> with this type of clause.  <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Realising there was no one at home</span>, I left the package on the porch.  </span><br/><br/> Both these types of sentence might begin with <span class=\"italic\">on</span> or <span class=\"italic\">upon</span>: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">On opening the envelope ... Upon realising ...  </span></li><br/>  <li>An event which is the result of another event <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I didn't get wet, <span class=\"strong\">having remembered to take my umbrella</span>. </li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Being a prompt and meticulous person, Jennifer was always very specific about any arrangements she made."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Realising that Alex was likely to forget, Jennifer reminded him to come on time."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Smiling to himself, Alex wondered how he and Jennifer could have managed to stay happily married all these years."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Feeling very annoyed, Alex went straight home. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Upon arriving home, Alex wasn't surprised to see that Jennifer had already arrived. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "prompt"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "done without delay; immediate"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Being a prompt and meticulous person, Jennifer was always very specific about any arrangements she made. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le08ob02aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you talk about personalities and relationships."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "meticulous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "showing great attention to detail; very careful and precise"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Being a prompt and meticulous person, Jennifer was always very specific about any arrangements she made. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le08ob02aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "easy-going"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "relaxed and tolerant "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Her husband Alex, on the other hand, was an easy-going fellow, who was usually late."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le08ob02aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to reproach"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to express disapproval or disappointment"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Before Jennifer could say a word, Alex reproached her, wit